    "updated_at": "2022-09-13T06:40:45Z",
    "body": "Historically, I believe Gecko implemented `document.open` by creating a new realm and then \"reparenting\" existing DOM node objects to the new realm. That logic is since long gone, and assuming there isn't anywhere else that could change the realm of an object (I cannot recall any) we should be able to remove it.",
